    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Daniel and Sol for the replies. Seems like the initial choice I provide comes from a very improbable part of the parameter space. I&#39;d try out both the options you suggested. <div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Abhi</div><div><br><div><br></div></div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Nov 2, 2016 at 9:31 PM, Daniel Turek <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">db...@williams.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Abhirup, thanks for your use of NIMBLE and sending your question to the list.  Right off hand I don&#39;t know why the block sampler isn&#39;t updating, but replacing the block sampler with 100 univariate RW samplers on the w[i] terms shows good mixing.  You can do that via:<div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">gpconf &lt;- configureMCMC(CgpModel, print=TRUE)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">##### changes begin here</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">gpconf$removeSamplers(&#39;w&#39;)<br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">for(node in gpModel$expandNodeNames(&#39;w&#39;, returnScalarComponents=TRUE)) {<br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">    gpconf$addSampler(node, &#39;RW&#39;)</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">}</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">gpconf$printSamplers()</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">##### changes end here</font></div><span><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">gpconf$addMonitors(c(&#39;w&#39;))<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">gpMCMC &lt;- buildMCMC(gpconf)<br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">CgpMCMC &lt;- compileNimble(gpMCMC, project = CgpModel)</font><br></div></span></div><div><br></div><div>Then the sampling looks good for the w[i] terms.</div><div><br></div><div>Let us know how that works for you.</div><div><br></div><div>Daniel</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><div><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, Nov 2, 2016 at 6:27 PM, Abhirup Datta <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">abhi...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m trying to run a simple random effect model but the random effect vectors are not updating even after running the MCMC long. Here is a MWE.</div><div><font color=\"#999999\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## model code ###</font></div><div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpCode &lt;- nimbleCode({</font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">    for(i in 1:n){ y[i] ~ dnorm(w[i],sd=tau)}</span><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">    Vw[,] &lt;- sigma*chol(G[,])</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">    w[] ~ dmnorm(muw[], cholesky=Vw[,], prec_param=0)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">    sigma ~ dunif(0, 100)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">    tau ~ dunif(0, 10)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">})</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">## data ###</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">set.seed(1)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">n=100</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">sigs=4</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">w=as.vector(rmvnorm(1,rep(0,n),sigs*0.5^as.matrix(dist(1:n))))</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Y=w+sqrt(0.5*sigs)*rnorm(n)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">### setting up nimble model ####</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpModel &lt;- nimbleModel(gpCode, constants = list(n = n, G=0.5^as.matrix(dist(1:n)), muw=rep(0,n)), </font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">    dimensions=list(y=n, Vw=c(n, n), w=n, Vy=c(n, n), G = c(n, n)), check=FALSE)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpModel$setData(list(y = Y))</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpModel$sigma &lt;- 1</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpModel$tau &lt;- 0.1</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpModel$w &lt;- rep(0,n)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">CgpModel &lt;- compileNimble(gpModel)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">### MCMC ####</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpconf &lt;- configureMCMC(CgpModel, print=TRUE)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpconf$addMonitors(c(&#39;w&#39;))<span style=\"white-space:pre-wrap\">\t</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpMCMC &lt;- buildMCMC(gpconf)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">CgpMCMC &lt;- compileNimble(gpMCMC, project = CgpModel)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Nmcmc=100000</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">set.seed(1)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">CgpMCMC$run(Nmcmc)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">gpMCMCsamples &lt;- as.matrix(CgpMCMC$mvSamples)</font></div><div><font color=\"#999999\" style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br></font></div><div><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font color=\"#999999\">plot(gpMCMCsamples[,&quot;w[1]&quot;]) </font> </span><font color=\"#ff0000\"> ### all values are 0 (same for all the other random effects)</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Is this just because the block RW Metropolis is slow for a 100-dimensional vector ? </span><font color=\"#000000\">Still no movement after 100000 iterations seem odd. </font><font color=\"#000000\">Also if I use </font><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">gpModel$w &lt;- rep(</span><font color=\"#ff0000\">1</font><span style=\"color:rgb(153,153,153)\">,n) </span><font color=\"#000000\">instead, I do see movements in the values of w&#39;s. </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Also how do I change the block RW for w to 100 univariate RWs, one for each w[i] ?</font></div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#ff0000\"><br></font></div></font></span></div><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;nimble-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nimble-users+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nimble...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/0d31f690-6be4-4450-9618-f3e18289ed4f%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/0d31f690-6be4-4450-9618-f3e18289ed4f%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792479171663000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0B6hCzD1pMtc1YinjSsci2\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/nimble-users/0d31f690-6be4-4450-9618-f3e18289ed4f%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792479171663000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00-a_9zqfTnS3QazosSWkT\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
